---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---
<SiteLayout title="saGraph — see what can move next" description="A local-first desktop task panel for workflows with dependencies. See what is ready, what is blocked, and why.">
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="hero container">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">A calmer way to finish work</p>
        <h1>Tasks that understand what comes next.</h1>
        <p class="lead">saGraph is a compact desktop task panel for workflows with real dependencies. See what is ready, what is blocked, and why.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/download">Download saGraph <span>↓</span></a><a class="button button-ghost" href="/docs">Read the docs</a></div>
        <p class="fine-print">Windows · Linux · macOS · Free trial available</p>
      </div>
      <div class="window-card" aria-label="saGraph interface preview">
        <div class="window-top"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>saGraph</span><span>⋯</span></div>
        <div class="window-body"><div class="mini-title">Today <span>4 tasks</span></div><div class="task done"><b>✓</b><span>Review project brief</span></div><div class="task ready"><b>→</b><span>Write implementation plan</span><em>Ready</em></div><div class="task blocked"><b>⊘</b><span>Ship first prototype</span><em>2 blockers</em></div><div class="task ready"><b>→</b><span>Send progress update</span><em>Ready</em></div></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="proof-section container">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">For work with a sequence</p><h2>Some tasks are not ready just because they are on your list.</h2><p class="section-intro">saGraph is for the moments when “what should I do next?” depends on more than priority. It keeps the prerequisites visible without turning your whole day into project-management administration.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="card feature"><span class="feature-icon">↳</span><h3>Make prerequisites explicit</h3><p>Write dependencies as AND, OR and NOT expressions. A task can wait for two things, either of two paths, or the absence of a blocker.</p></article>
        <article class="card feature"><span class="feature-icon">◌</span><h3>Stay close to the work</h3><p>The compact panel can stay on top while you work in another app. Check off a task without opening a project dashboard.</p></article>
        <article class="card feature"><span class="feature-icon">⌘</span><h3>Investigate the blockage</h3><p>Open the dependency graph when a task is locked. Follow the chain instead of guessing which prerequisite is holding it back.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="workflow-section container">
      <div class="workflow-copy"><p class="eyebrow">A small example</p><h2>From “blocked” to a useful next step.</h2><p>Imagine a release workflow. “Publish update” depends on a signed build and a passing smoke test. saGraph does not try to plan the release for you; it makes the condition visible.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs">See how dependencies work <span>→</span></a></div>
      <div class="card workflow-card" aria-label="Example dependency workflow"><div class="workflow-node complete"><span>✓</span><div><strong>Build release</strong><small>Done</small></div></div><div class="workflow-line"></div><div class="workflow-node ready"><span>→</span><div><strong>Run smoke test</strong><small>Ready</small></div></div><div class="workflow-line"></div><div class="workflow-node blocked"><span>!</span><div><strong>Publish update</strong><small>Waiting for smoke test</small></div></div></div>
    </section>
    <section class="details-section container"><div class="detail-grid"><article><p class="eyebrow">Local first</p><h3>Your task data stays on your machine.</h3><p>saGraph is a desktop application with local data files and portable-mode support. The website handles downloads, licensing, and release information; it is not your task database.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Built for interruption</p><h3>Useful in the gaps between other apps.</h3><p>Keep the panel visible, make a quick change, then get back to your editor, terminal, or browser. It is deliberately smaller than a full project-management suite.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Early release</p><h3>Small, focused, and still growing.</h3><p>Version 0.1.0 has the core workflow in place. Some platform-specific validation and documentation are still being expanded openly.</p></article></div></section>
    <section class="cta container card"><div><p class="eyebrow">Try the real workflow</p><h2>Keep the next step visible.</h2><p>Download the desktop panel and start with one workflow that has a real dependency.</p></div><a class="button button-primary" href="/download">Download saGraph <span>↗</span></a></section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</SiteLayout>
<style>
  .hero { align-items: center; display: grid; gap: 5rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.82fr; min-height: 650px; padding: 5rem 0; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 7vw, 6.4rem); letter-spacing: -0.045em; line-height: 0.95; margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem; max-width: 700px; }
  .lead { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.7; max-width: 510px; }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .fine-print { color: #77738b; font-size: 0.75rem; margin-top: 1.3rem; }
  .window-card { background: #151722; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16); border-radius: 22px; box-shadow: 0 30px 100px rgba(92, 78, 210, 0.24); overflow: hidden; transform: rotate(2deg); }
  .window-top { align-items: center; background: #1c1e2b; color: #aaa7bb; display: flex; font-size: 0.7rem; justify-content: space-between; padding: 0.8rem 1rem; }
  .dots { display: flex; gap: 0.28rem; }.dots i { background: #706b83; border-radius: 99px; height: 6px; width: 6px; }
  .window-body { padding: 1.2rem; }.mini-title { color: #f4f1ff; display: flex; font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 700; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 1rem; }.mini-title span { color: #77738b; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 400; }
  .task { align-items: center; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.07); color: #d8d5e5; display: flex; font-size: 0.75rem; gap: 0.65rem; padding: 1rem 0.2rem; }.task b { border-radius: 50%; color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.9rem; }.task.done { color: #77738b; text-decoration: line-through; }.task.blocked b, .task.blocked em { color: #f29aab; }.task em { color: var(--cyan); font-size: 0.65rem; font-style: normal; margin-left: auto; }
  .proof-section, .workflow-section, .details-section { padding: 7rem 0 0; }.section-heading { max-width: 760px; }.section-heading h2, .workflow-copy h2, .cta h2 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem); letter-spacing: -0.06em; line-height: 1; margin: 0.8rem 0 1.2rem; }.section-intro, .workflow-copy p, .details-section p, .cta p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 650px; }.feature-grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); margin-top: 2.5rem; }.feature { padding: 1.6rem; }.feature-icon { color: var(--accent); font-size: 1.6rem; }.feature h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 1.8rem 0 0.6rem; }.feature p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0; }
  .workflow-section { align-items: center; display: grid; gap: 5rem; grid-template-columns: 0.9fr 1.1fr; }.workflow-copy h2 { max-width: 520px; }.workflow-copy > p:not(.eyebrow) { margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }.text-link { color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 700; }.text-link span { display: inline-block; margin-left: 0.3rem; transition: transform 0.2s ease; }.text-link:hover span { transform: translateX(4px); }.workflow-card { padding: 1.5rem; }.workflow-node { align-items: center; display: flex; gap: 0.8rem; padding: 0.9rem; }.workflow-node > span { align-items: center; border: 1px solid currentColor; border-radius: 50%; display: inline-flex; flex: 0 0 28px; font-weight: 800; height: 28px; justify-content: center; width: 28px; }.workflow-node strong, .workflow-node small { display: block; }.workflow-node strong { font-size: 0.92rem; }.workflow-node small { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.72rem; margin-top: 0.25rem; }.workflow-node.complete { color: var(--cyan); }.workflow-node.ready { color: var(--accent); }.workflow-node.blocked { color: #f29aab; }.workflow-line { border-left: 1px dashed var(--line); height: 1.2rem; margin-left: 1.75rem; }.details-section { padding-bottom: 1rem; }.detail-grid { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); display: grid; gap: 2rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); padding-top: 2rem; }.detail-grid h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 0.8rem 0 0.4rem; }.detail-grid p:not(.eyebrow) { font-size: 0.88rem; margin: 0; }.cta { align-items: center; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 6rem; padding: 2rem 2.2rem; }.cta h2 { margin-bottom: 0; max-width: 570px; }.cta p { margin: 0.8rem 0 0; max-width: 530px; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .hero { gap: 3rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr; min-height: 0; padding: 5rem 0 3rem; }.window-card { max-width: 520px; transform: none; }.feature-grid, .detail-grid, .workflow-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }.workflow-section { gap: 2.5rem; }.cta { align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem; } }
</style>
